window.DH=window.DH||{};window.DH["e02"]={"id":"e02","title":"第二集","parts":[{"id":"p01","title":"Gabrielle 出轨差点被发现","lines":[{"id":"e02p0101","s":"Alice","t":"An odd thing happens when we die. Our senses vanish.","r":true,"m":["odd adj. 奇怪的，反常的；偶然出现的；奇形怪状的，各种各样的；奇数的；","vanish v. 突然不见，消失；不复存在，灭绝；","senses: Taste, touch, smell, sound, sight 五感:味觉/触觉/嗅觉/听觉/视觉"]},{"id":"e02p0102","s":"Alice","t":"Taste, touch, smell, and sound become a distant memory, but our sight -- ah, our sight expands.","r":true,"m":["distant adj. 遥远的，久远的；冷淡的；远亲的；不同的","expand v. 扩大，增加；扩展，发展；细谈，详述；"]},{"id":"e02p0103","s":"Alice","t":"And we can suddenly see the world we've left behind so clearly.","r":true,"m":["left behind 被遗留"]},{"id":"e02p0104","s":"Alice","t":"Of course, most of what's visible to the dead could also be seen by the living, if they only take the time to look.","r":true,"m":["most of what's visible to the dead 死者能看到的大部分东西(这里是what引导的介宾从句，what在从句中充当主语) = most of the things that are visible to the dead","the dead 死者 the living 生者，活着的人们","take the time to 花足够的时间来做某事，做得好或仔细"]},{"id":"e02p0105","s":"Alice","t":"Like my friend Gabrielle, I should have seen how unhappy she was, but I didn't.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0106","s":"Alice","t":"I only saw her clothes from Paris, and her platinum jewelry, and her brand-new diamond watch.","r":true,"m":["platinum n. 铂，白金；adj. 铂的，白金的；","jewelry/jewellery n. 珠宝，首饰","brand-new adj.崭新的，未用过的；最近获得的 brand n.品牌，商标；"]},{"id":"e02p0107","s":"Alice","t":"Had I looked closer, I’d have seen that Gabrielle was a drowning woman, desperately in search of a life raft.","r":true,"m":["Had I looked closer == If I had looked closer 虚拟倒装","I’d have seen == I would have seen 侧重结果的将会发生，口语连读就是I'd've seen","drown v. （声音）压过，盖过；沉浸于，淹没于；（使）淹死","in search of 试图寻找或寻求 = search for != find 找到","raft n. 木排，木筏； 橡皮艇，充气船； life raft 救生筏"]},{"id":"e02p0108","s":"Alice","t":"Luckily for her, she found one. Of course, Gabrielle only saw her young gardener as a way to infuse her life with a little excitement.","r":true,"m":["see sb as a way to do sth 把某人看作是做某事的一种途径 / 方式","infuse v. 使充满（某种感觉），向…灌输；冲泡（茶、药草等），浸渍；输注","infuse ... with ... 用… 注入…；使… 充满…"]},{"id":"e02p0109","s":"Alice","t":"But now she was about to discover just how exciting her life could get.","r":true,"m":["be about to 即将要做某事"]},{"id":"e02p0110","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Damn it. Come on! Hurry up! Let's go.","r":false,"m":["damn 该死，见鬼 严厉批评，谴责；Damn it 该死！"]},{"id":"e02p0111","s":"John","t":"Where are the rest of my clothes?","r":true,"m":["the rest of 名词：剩余的……、剩下的……"]},{"id":"e02p0112","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I'll find them. Just get out. Out the window. ... Hey, honey. You're home early.","r":true,"m":["You're home early：用于当看到某人已经在家，而且比平常预期的时间要早的时候发出的一种感慨、疑问或者简单陈述","You get home early：描述规律性的行为或具体的动作情况，比如谈论日常的生活作息，或讲述某一天具体到家时间比较早的行为"]},{"id":"e02p0113","s":"Carlos","t":"My meeting got canceled. Didn't you take a shower this morning?","r":true,"m":["cancel => cancelled/canceled v. 取消；宣布作废","My meeting got canceled. 这里的‘get + 过去分词’构成的被动结构，比‘be + 过去分词’的被动更口语化","take a shower v. 洗澡；洗浴 have/take a bath 泡澡"]},{"id":"e02p0114","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I just finished a workout.","r":true,"m":["workout n. 锻炼，训练；试验；作为锻炼讲时，是可数名词"]},{"id":"e02p0115","s":"Carlos","t":"Where's John? That's his truck out front.","r":true,"m":["truck n. 卡车，载重汽车；手推车"]},{"id":"e02p0116","s":"Alice","t":"Gabrielle was panicked. She knew if her husband discovered her secret, she would feel the full force of his wrath.","r":true,"m":["panicked v. 使恐慌（panic 的过去式和过去分词）= in a panic","full force 全部的威力、强烈程度","wrath n. 愤怒，盛怒 full force of his wrath 他满腔怒火的全部杀伤力","后面一句是虚拟语气，对现在的虚拟：if + 一般过去时（were/did）→ 主句用 would/could/might do"]},{"id":"e02p0117","s":"John","t":"Hey, Mr. Solis.","r":false},{"id":"e02p0118","s":"Carlos","t":"Hey, John, did you take care of that ficus yet?","r":true,"m":["ficus n. 榕树; 热带榕属植物"]},{"id":"e02p0119","s":"John","t":"I'll get to it as soon as I'm done here.","r":true,"m":["get to 开始，着手; 到达，抵达; 理解，明白","I'll get to it as soon as I'm done here.我在这里的事一做完，就会着手去做它"]},{"id":"e02p0120","s":"Carlos","t":"Alright. We need to talk about the hedges later.","r":false,"m":["hedge n. 树篱；防范措施，防备手段 hedge risk 对冲风险"]},{"id":"e02p0121","s":"Alice","t":"But she was quickly reminded that what Carlos couldn't see couldn't hurt her.","r":true,"m":["that 引导的宾语从句，本来that可省，但这一句中宾语从句里面还嵌套别的从句（what/who 从句）：that 尽量不省略，消除断句歧义","what Carlos couldn't see couldn't hurt her. 单看这个从句，其中的 what 引导的是一个主语从句"]}]},{"id":"p02","title":"主妇们讨论给 Alice 的信","lines":[{"id":"e02p0201","s":"Alice","t":"The peaceful facade of Wisteria Lane had recently been shattered, first by my suicide, and then by the discovery of a note among my belongings that suggested a suspicious reason for my desperate act.","r":true,"m":["facade n. 假象，伪装;（建筑物的）正面，立面","shatter v. 破碎，碎裂；破坏；使极为惊愕难过 n. 碎片；受到极大打击的状态","of a 在美式口语中是高频连读组合，核心发音会弱读成 /əvə/","suggest v. 暗示，暗指；提议，建议；表明","suspicious adj. 感觉可疑的，怀疑的；不信任的。现代英语里，suspect 主流只有两种词性：动词/名词，作形容词非常罕见","a reason for... 是常见搭配，…的原因"]},{"id":"e02p0202","s":"Alice","t":"My friends gathered to discuss its implications.","r":true,"m":["implication n. 可能的影响（或作用、结果）；含意，暗指；牵连，涉及"]},{"id":"e02p0203","s":"Susan","t":"I think we should give it to Paul.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0204","s":"Gabrielle","t":"He's still mourning, Susan. He'll probably freak out.","r":true,"m":["mourn v. 悼念，哀悼；对……感到痛心","freak out 使崩溃；极度不安 freak v.吃惊，不安，恼怒；"]},{"id":"e02p0205","s":"Susan","t":"It doesn't matter. She was his wife. He deserves to have all the facts.","r":true,"m":["It doesn't matter. 没关系","Sorry: That’s okay./ That’s all right. / Don’t worry about it. "]},{"id":"e02p0206","s":"Bree","t":"Well, we could do it gently. We could tell him about it over coffee and pastry.","r":true,"m":["gently adv. 文静地，温柔地；轻柔地；渐进地，平缓地；","over 介词：在…期间；一边…一边…，替代 while we are having... 冗长句式","pastry n. 油酥面团；酥皮糕点"]},{"id":"e02p0207","s":"Lynette","t":"That would be fun. \"Paul, we have proof your wife killed herself over some deep, dark secret. Another bear claw?\"","r":true,"m":["proof n. 证明，证据；检验，证实 不可数名词","over some deep, dark secret. over 介词：因……；由于（表原因）","bear claw 熊爪：一种填充面点 claw n.（动物的）爪，爪子；"]},{"id":"e02p0208","s":"Gabrielle","t":"We could always call the police.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0209","s":"Lynette","t":"Maybe it's just some sort of sick joke.","r":true,"m":["some sort of + 名词 = a kind of 某一种、某种 sort of 副词短语,有点、稍微、算得上","sick joke 恶心的笑话，恶毒的玩笑"]},{"id":"e02p0210","s":"Bree","t":"Well, if it was a joke, it was in very poor taste.","r":true,"m":["if it was a joke 是条件状语从句，表示假设的情况","poor taste 品味差 in poor taste 不得体：令人不悦或愤怒的方式"]},{"id":"e02p0211","s":"Susan","t":"No, this was serious. I know it was. We got to find out what was going on.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0212","s":"Lynette","t":"Let's say we do; there's a chance we're not going to like what we find.","r":true,"m":["Let's say we do. 假设我们这样做。这句话通常用于提出一个假设或推测，然后探讨在这种假设下可能发生的情况或结果。","chance n. 可能性； 机会，时机；危险，冒险；运气，偶然","there's a chance that ...  存在…… 的可能性","There's a chance we're not going to like what we find. 我们有可能不会喜欢我们所发现的。"]},{"id":"e02p0213","s":"Susan","t":"Well, isn't it worse to be in the dark? I mean, imagine she did all these horrible things.","r":true,"m":["isn't it worse to be in the dark? 处在不知情的状态下难道不是更糟糕吗？","to be in the dark 在黑暗中，还常引申为蒙在鼓里；不知情","horrible adj. 可怕的，令人恐惧的；糟糕的 terrible"]},{"id":"e02p0214","s":"Bree","t":"It's the age-old question. isn't it? How much do we really want to know about our neighbors?","r":true,"m":["age-old 古老的；由来已久的"]},{"id":"e02p0215","s":"Alice","t":"My friends were right to be concerned; they knew that every family has its secrets.","r":true,"m":["My friends were right to be concerned. 朋友们的担心是对的。It's right to be nervous. 紧张是正常的","be right to 正确的，合适的，恰当的","sb be concerned about sth 某人对某事感到担心 sth concern sb 某事使某人担心"]},{"id":"e02p0216","s":"Alice","t":"And as my son and husband could have told them, you need to think carefully before digging them up.","r":true,"m":["could have told 本可以告诉（实际没说）","dig up 挖掘；发现（秘密）"]},{"id":"e02p0217","s":"Alice","t":"After talking for hours, my friends still hadn't agreed on what to do with the note.","r":true,"m":["talk for hours 聊了好几个小时","agree on 就某事达成共识","do with + 物品：处理、处置某物"]},{"id":"e02p0218","s":"Alice","t":"So they decided to talk about it in the morning after a good night's rest. But no one could fall asleep that night.","r":true,"m":["a good night's rest 好好睡一觉","fall asleep 入睡 asleep adj.睡着的；麻木的，发麻的；"]},{"id":"e02p0219","s":"Alice","t":"They each kept thinking of my suicide and how terribly alone I must have felt. ","r":true,"m":["keep doing sth 持续不停地做某事、一直反复做","alone adj. 独自的（强调状态），做形容词的时候只能做表语，不能做前置定语","lonely adj. 孤独的（强调情绪）"]},{"id":"e02p0220","s":"Alice","t":"You see, loneliness was something my friends understood all too well.","r":true,"m":["loneliness n. 孤独，寂寞","understand all too well 太明白了 all too well = 感同身受，再清楚不过"]}]},{"id":"p03","title":"Bree 提出见婚姻顾问","lines":[{"id":"e02p0301","s":"Rex","t":"It's okay. I'm up.","r":true,"m":["I'm up 我起床了 I'm going to bed 我要睡觉了"]},{"id":"e02p0302","s":"Bree","t":"Good. I have a question for you. Do you remember when you proposed?","r":true,"m":["remember when you did… 记得做某事的那个时刻"]},{"id":"e02p0303","s":"Rex","t":"For God's sake.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0304","s":"Bree","t":"We sat on Skyline Drive and drank a bottle of apple wine.","r":true,"m":["Skyline Drive 天际线公路 Drive 大道","a bottle of 一瓶"]},{"id":"e02p0305","s":"Bree","t":"And when we finished it, you turned to me, and you said, \"If you marry me, Bree Mason, I promise to love you for the rest of my life.\"","r":true,"m":["finish sth：把某物喝完、吃完、做完"]},{"id":"e02p0306","s":"Bree","t":"And even though I was engaged to Ty Grant, and even though my father didn't like you, I said yes.","r":true,"m":["even though 尽管，虽然; 即使，纵然","engaged  adj. 已订婚的；从事……的，忙于……的；电话占线的； engage v.雇用，聘请；参加，从事；吸引，引起；与……交战，开战；","be engaged to sb 与某人订婚","be engaged with sb 与某人交涉、接洽","be engaged in sth 忙于某事"]},{"id":"e02p0307","s":"Rex","t":"That was a long time ago.","r":true,"m":["a long time ago 很久以前","That was a long time ago. 那是很久以前的事了"]},{"id":"e02p0308","s":"Bree","t":"You're going to cancel the meeting with that divorce lawyer, and we're going to find ourselves a marriage counselor.","r":true,"m":["counselor n. 顾问，咨询师；律师，法律顾问"]},{"id":"e02p0309","s":"Bree","t":"You promised.","r":false},{"id":"e02p0310","s":"Rex","t":"All right.","r":false},{"id":"e02p0311","s":"Bree","t":"Good. I'm going to make myself some warm milk. Would you like something to drink?","r":true,"m":["make myself sth 给自己弄点……"]},{"id":"e02p0312","s":"Rex","t":"Anything but apple wine.","r":true,"m":["Anything but sth 除……之外什么都行"]}]},{"id":"p04","title":"Julie 和 Susan 夜晚闲聊","lines":[{"id":"e02p0401","s":"Alice","t":"Susan awoke that night alone and parched, but as she gazed out of her window, she saw the tall drink of water she needed to quench her thirst.","r":true,"m":["wake vi/vt. 唤醒，醒来；唤起 → woke → woken（口语常用 wake up）","awake vi/vt.（使）醒来；唤起 adj.醒着的 → awoke → awoken（文学/旁白常用）","awaken vi/vt. 唤醒；唤起（抽象事物，正式用词）→ awakened → awakened","parch v. 烤，烘 parched adj. 焦的；炎热的；炒过的；干透的；非常口渴的","gaze v. 凝视，注视","the tall drink of water 俚语，形容高大英俊的男人","quench one's thirst 解渴 quench v. 止渴；满足"]},{"id":"e02p0402","s":"Julie","t":"\"Dear diary, Mike doesn't even know I'm alive.\"","r":true,"m":["Dear diary 日记常用开头","doesn't even know 甚至都不知道；助动词 ➜ even ➜ 实义动词"]},{"id":"e02p0403","s":"Susan","t":"Shut up.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0404","s":"Julie","t":"If you want to date him, you're going to have to ask him out.","r":true,"m":["date sb 和某人约会","ask sb out 约某人出去","be going to have to do sth 将要不得不做某事"]},{"id":"e02p0405","s":"Susan","t":"I keep hoping he'll ask me out.","r":true,"m":["keep hoping 一直希望 I keep hoping that ... 我一直希望……；持续期望着……"]},{"id":"e02p0406","s":"Julie","t":"How's that going?","r":true,"m":["How's that going? 进展如何？那进行得怎么样了？"]},{"id":"e02p0407","s":"Susan","t":"Shouldn't you be making brownies for your nerdy friends?","r":true,"m":["Shouldn't you be doing sth? 你难道不该在做某事吗？","brownie n. 布朗尼蛋糕","nerdy adj. 书呆子气的"]},{"id":"e02p0408","s":"Julie","t":"I can't find the measuring cup. Have you seen it?","r":true,"m":[" measuring cup 量杯 measure v. 测量"]},{"id":"e02p0409","s":"Susan","t":"The measuring cup? Well, it's got to be here somewhere. Just keep looking.","r":true,"m":["it's got to be here somewhere 它一定在这里的某个地方 it's got to be = it has got to be 一定是","somewhere 某个地方"]}]},{"id":"p05","title":"Gabrielle 和 Carlos 又吵架","lines":[{"id":"e02p0501","s":"Carlos","t":"I know you're awake.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0502","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I know you're a jerk.","r":true,"m":["jerk n. 混蛋、讨人厌的人"]},{"id":"e02p0503","s":"Carlos","t":"Dinner with Tanaka ran long. I'm sorry.","r":true,"m":["run long 固定口语：（会议 / 饭局）拖得很久、超时"]},{"id":"e02p0504","s":"Gabrielle","t":"You know, Carlos, I didn't marry you so I could have dinner by myself 6 times a week.","r":true,"m":["I didn't marry you so I could have dinner by myself. 我嫁给你可不是为了一周有六天都自己一个人吃晚饭。","主语 +  don't /didn't + 动作 + so (that) +  主语 +  （不希望发生的）结果 / 状态翻译时，一律译为：我做某事，才不是为了…","I didn't do A so I could do B，是英语里表达 **“我做 A，才不是为了 B”** 的经典句式。","I didn't marry you so I could go to Paris. 这种句式有天热的歧义，完全依靠语境判断"]},{"id":"e02p0505","s":"Gabrielle","t":"You know how bored I was today? I came this close to actually cleaning the house.","r":true,"m":["come close to doing sth 差点做某事；接近做某事。在这里，“to” 是一个介词，而不是不定式符号，所以后面要接动名词形式（doing）。"]},{"id":"e02p0506","s":"Carlos","t":"Don't be that way. I got you a gift.","r":true,"m":["Don't be that way 别这样"]},{"id":"e02p0507","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Nope. You're not going to buy your way out of this one.","r":true,"m":["buy your way out of sth 通过花钱的方式从…中脱身；靠花钱来摆脱…"]},{"id":"e02p0508","s":"Carlos","t":"It's a good gift.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0509","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Is that white gold?","r":true,"m":["white gold 白金 platinum 铂金，更稀有 → 价格远高于 white gold"]},{"id":"e02p0510","s":"Carlos","t":"Yeah. Put it on and then make love to me.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0511","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I'm not in the mood. But we could stay up and talk.","r":true,"m":["in the mood 心情好，有兴致","stay up 熬夜"]},{"id":"e02p0512","s":"Carlos","t":"When a man buys a woman expensive jewelry, there are many things he may want in return, for future reference, conversation ain't one of them.","r":true,"m":["buy sb sth（双宾语）= buy sth for sb","in return 作为回报","for future reference 供以后参考 reference n. 提及，谈到；参考，查阅；引言，引文；","ain't 不是；没有非正式的缩写，通常用于英语口语中，是am not、is not、are not、has not 或 have not的缩写形式。"]},{"id":"e02p0513","s":"Carlos","t":"Hey, that was a joke. What the hell is wrong with you?","r":true,"m":["What the hell is wrong with you? 你到底怎么回事？hell n. 地狱；苦难的经历"]},{"id":"e02p0514","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Let go of me.","r":true,"m":["Let go of me 放开我,松手！ let me go更强调我想要离开的意愿，而let go of me更强调你应该放开我的动作。"]},{"id":"e02p0515","s":"Carlos","t":"You've been acting like a nightmare for a month. What's wrong? I can't fix it unless you tell me.","r":true,"m":["have been doing 现在完成进行时：一直在做某事：表示过去某个时间点开始做某事，并一直持续到现在。","nightmare n. 噩梦；可怕的经历"]},{"id":"e02p0516","s":"Gabrielle","t":"It's not exciting anymore, Carlos.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0517","s":"Carlos","t":"So what am I supposed to do?","r":true,"m":["what am I supposed to do? 我应该做什么？我该怎么办？"]},{"id":"e02p0518","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I don't know. Be the way you used to be. Surprise me. Take my breath away.","r":true,"m":["Be the way you used to be 做回你曾经的样子 way = 行事方式、样子、状态","take one’s breath away 使大吃一惊 breath: 呼吸"]},{"id":"e02p0519","s":"Carlos","t":"Okay.","r":false}]},{"id":"p06","title":"Mike 邀 Susan 共进晚餐","lines":[{"id":"e02p0601","s":"Susan","t":"I didn't realize anybody was going to be out here. I just sort of rolled out of bed.","r":true,"m":["was going to 过去将来时 would + 动词原形 / was/were going to + 动词原形","roll out of bed （睡眼惺忪地）从床上翻身起来，一骨碌从床上爬起来"]},{"id":"e02p0602","s":"Mike","t":"I'm sure you look fine. Oh, Bongo, stop. Sorry, he scares easy.","r":true,"m":["he scares easy 他很容易受到惊吓，美式口语非正式用法 = he gets scared easily"]},{"id":"e02p0603","s":"Susan","t":"No, it's fine. I get it.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0604","s":"Mike","t":"I didn't mean to disturb you. I'll see you later.","r":true,"m":["mean to 打算，计划","disturb v. 打扰，妨碍；使焦虑，使烦恼；移动，弄乱"]},{"id":"e02p0605","s":"Susan","t":"Do you want to have dinner with me?","r":true},{"id":"e02p0606","s":"Mike","t":"Just the two of us?","r":true,"m":["Just the two of us (the可以省略) 就我们两个;two of us 我们之中两个人"]},{"id":"e02p0607","s":"Susan","t":"Well, and Julie. It's a thing we do when somebody new moves into the neighborhood, we invite them over for a home-cooked meal. Sort of a tradition.","r":true,"m":["It's a thing we do when... 这是我们在…时会做的事","a home-cooked meal 家常菜（具体一餐） home cooking（抽象）","sort of a tradition 算是一种传统","sort of 有点儿，有几分;口语化的表达"]},{"id":"e02p0608","s":"Mike","t":"I thought you said you were a lousy cook.","r":true,"m":["lousy adj. 差劲的；不擅长的"]},{"id":"e02p0609","s":"Susan","t":"Well, I order takeout.","r":true,"m":["takeout n. 外卖 order takeout 点外卖 get takeout"]},{"id":"e02p0610","s":"Mike","t":"You invite them over for home cooking and give them takeout?","r":true},{"id":"e02p0611","s":"Susan","t":"Yeah, it's sort of a new tradition. I'm working out the kinks.","r":true,"m":["I'm working out the kinks. 我还在磨合调整","work out 调试、磨合；解决，算出，制定","kink n. 奇想；扭结；蜷缩；（计划、安排中的）小故障、小麻烦。"]},{"id":"e02p0612","s":"Mike","t":"I'll tell you what. How about I cook? And you guys come over to my place. Friday night at six?","r":true,"m":["I'll tell you what. 我有个主意","come over to my place 来我家","Friday night at six 周五晚上六点"]},{"id":"e02p0613","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, great. I'll be there. By, Bongo.","r":false},{"id":"e02p0614","s":"Susan","t":"Julie!  Mike Delfino just invited us to dinner Friday night.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0615","s":"Julie","t":"He did? Cool.","r":false},{"id":"e02p0616","s":"Susan","t":"But only I'm going because you're gonna come down with something semi-serious that requires bed rest and fluids.","r":true,"m":["come down with 染上（疾病）","semi-serious 比较严重的，不轻不重的（semi-: 部分的，半、轻度）","bed rest and fluids 卧床休息和补液"]},{"id":"e02p0617","s":"Alice","t":"Julie was glad Susan was rekindling her love life. Of course, she was unaware of her mother's recent track record with fire.","r":true,"m":["rekindle v. 重新点燃 kindle v. 点燃，开始燃烧；激起，激发；","be unaware of sth 没有意识到某事；不知道某事；未察觉到某事","track record with 在…方面的过往表现、历史记录、履历情况 track record with fire 纵火的前科"]}]},{"id":"p07","title":"Eddie 整理火灾现场","lines":[{"id":"e02p0701","s":"Eddie","t":"It's all gone. Everything my ex-husband worked for all those years gone.","r":true,"m":["It's all gone.全都没了；一切都消失了；全都不见了","all those years 那些年；这么多年；所有那些年","Everything ...(is) gone 属于口语 / 文学省略"]},{"id":"e02p0702","s":"Huber","t":"Don't worry about clothing. I already started a collection from people in the neighborhood.","r":true,"m":["clothing n. 衣服，衣物统称，侧重衣物这一类物资 == clothes","collection n. 收藏品，收集物；募捐；一堆"]},{"id":"e02p0703","s":"Eddie","t":"What? I don't want to wear other people's old crap.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0704","s":"Huber","t":"Eddie, you can be homeless or you can be ungracious. You really can't afford to be both.","r":true,"m":["ungracious adj. 无礼貌的，没规矩的；没有教养的；讨厌的","gracious adj. 有礼貌的，和蔼的；豪华舒适的，富足安逸的"]},{"id":"e02p0705","s":"Eddie","t":"That reminds me. My insurance check still hasn't come yet. Could I stay with you a few more weeks?","r":true,"m":["That reminds me.这倒提醒我了；那让我想起来了","insurance n. 保险；保险费；保险业；","check n. 支票(美式) == cheque(英式)","a few more weeks 再多几周 a few more 再多一些"]},{"id":"e02p0706","s":"Huber","t":"Of course. What kind of Christian would I be if I denied shelter to a friend in need?","r":true,"m":["What kind of person would I be if ...如果…… 我会是怎样的一个人啊","What kind of... 是一个疑问词组，在句中作表语，用于询问种类。","Christian n. 基督徒，信徒 Christmas 圣诞节","deny  v. 否认；拒绝承认；拒绝给予","shelter n. 居所，住处；遮蔽物，庇护处v. 提供庇护，提供保护；躲避，避难","deny shelter to sb 拒绝为某人提供住所；不给某人提供庇护 (反：offer shelter to sb)","sb in need 有需要的某人；处于困境中的某人"]},{"id":"e02p0707","s":"Huber","t":"Oh, look. Here's something we can salvage. Your measuring cup. We can just scrape off the burnt part and it'll look good as new.","r":true,"m":["salvage n. 抢救，救援；  v. 打捞，抢救；挽救","scrape off 刮掉  scrape v.（用小刀等）刮除；（使）刮擦；擦伤，刮坏","look (as) good as new 看上去完好如新 as good as 几乎等于，差不多等于"]},{"id":"e02p0708","s":"Eddie","t":"That's not my cup. Mine was plastic.","r":true,"m":["plastic cup 塑料制的 plastic surgery 整形手术 plastic suburban housewife 人造的，不自然的 -> 虚伪做作"]},{"id":"e02p0709","s":"Huber","t":"Well, how did it get in here?","r":true},{"id":"e02p0710","s":"Eddie","t":"I don't know. Who cares? Now, could you put that down and start looking for jewelry?","r":true}]},{"id":"p08","title":"婚姻顾问 Goldfine 出场","lines":[{"id":"e02p0801","s":"Alice","t":"Dr. Albert Goldfine was the most accomplished marriage counselor in the city.","r":true,"m":["accomplished adj. 造诣深厚的、资深的，熟练的，才华高的；娴于社交的；v. 完成，实现（accomplish 的过去式和过去分词）"]},{"id":"e02p0802","s":"Alice","t":"He had dealt with problems ranging from substance abuse to infidelity, to domestic violence.","r":true,"m":["range from ... to ... 范围从……到……","substance abuse 吸毒,物质滥用  substance n. 物质，材料；主旨；重要性；真实性，可信性；毒品；财产；实质， abuse v/n. 虐待；滥用，辜负；辱骂","infidelity n. 无信仰，不信神；背信；不忠行为，婚外情","domestic violence 家庭暴力"]},{"id":"e02p0803","s":"Alice","t":"Yes, Dr. Goldfine thought he had seen it all. And then he met the Van De Kamps.","r":true,"m":["see it all 看尽一切，习语：见过大世面、什么怪事都见识过"]},{"id":"e02p0804","s":"Bree","t":"Hi. I'm Bree. And this is my husband Rex. And I brought you some homemade potpourri.","r":true,"m":["homemade adj. 自制的，家里做的（被动含义：在家被制作出来）homemaking n.操持家务、家政（主动动作：打理家庭）homemaker n. 家庭主妇 / 主夫","a home-cooked meal 家常菜（具体一餐）home-cooked adj.家常的 home cooking n.家常菜（抽象）","ed → 形容词，描述做好的成品 ing → 名词，描述“制作” 这个行为","已经被词典收录、固化单词 → 直接连写：homemade /homemaking 名词 + 过去分词 临时组合形容词 → 加连字符：home-cooked 两个独立名词构成普通短语 → 空格分开：home cooking","potpourri n. 百花香；混合物；杂曲；大杂烩"]},{"id":"e02p0805","s":"Rex","t":"The answer is yes. You're about to make a fortune off us.","r":true,"m":["The answer is yes. 答案是肯定的","be about to 即将要做某事","make a fortune off us 从我们身上赚大钱 make sth off sb 从某人身上抢走某物 make a fortune 发财，赚大钱","fortune n. 时运，命运；好运，机遇；财富，巨款；未来，前途"]}]},{"id":"p09","title":"Lynette 被交警拦下","lines":[{"id":"e02p0901","s":"Lynette","t":"Boys! Guys, I'm begging you. Sit in your seats. I'm not gonna tell you again. Buckle up. I mean it, so help me... Oh, Crap!","r":true,"m":["I'm begging you 我求求你","sit in your seats 坐在你的座位上 sit on the chair 坐在椅子（板面）上","buckle up 扣安全带 buckle v. 发软；屈服；（使）弯曲；扣住 n. 搭扣","I'm not gonna tell you again. I’m only going to say this once.","I mean it 我是认真的","so help me 我发誓；老天作证"]},{"id":"e02p0902","s":"Officer","t":"License and registration, please. Ma'am, you know why I pulled you over?","r":true,"m":["License and registration 驾照和车辆登记证 License n. 执照，许可证；特许 registration n. 登记，注册，挂号；登记证，注册证；","Ma'am n. 女士；夫人，太太；小姐 ma'am = madam（口语缩略读音）","pull over 靠边停车 pull you over 拦下你"]},{"id":"e02p0903","s":"Lynette","t":"I have a theory.","r":true,"m":["I have a theory 我有种猜测 / 我有个推断 theory n.学说，理论"]},{"id":"e02p0904","s":"Officer","t":"The kids are jumping up and down, they should be sitting, wearing seat belts.","r":true,"m":["jump up and down 上下跳跃","should be doing sth 应该正在做某事","seat belt 座椅安全带  belt n.腰带，皮带；传送带；地带","wear a seat belt 系着安全带（状态） buckle up / put on a seat belt 系安全带（动作）"]},{"id":"e02p0905","s":"Lynette","t":"I yelled at them. They never listen to me. It's very frustrating.","r":true,"m":["yell at 大声责骂，呵斥 yell v.叫喊，大喊","frustrate v. 使懊恼，使沮丧；挫败，阻挠；受挫 I'm frustrated. "]},{"id":"e02p0906","s":"Officer","t":"You’re gonna hafta find a way to control them. After all, that's your job.","r":true,"m":["hafta <主美口>=have to","After all 毕竟"]},{"id":"e02p0907","s":"Alice","t":"Though he'd been a policeman for six years, officer Hayes had never found himself in a truly dangerous situation.","r":true,"m":["policeman n. 警察，警员","officer n. 军官；官员，高级职员；警察，警官；船长；Officer + 姓氏：警官 XX，美式最通用称呼，不分巡官、交警。"]},{"id":"e02p0908","s":"Alice","t":"Then again, he had never before told a woman how to raise her children.","r":true,"m":["Then again 另一方面；话说回来","raise v. 抚养，养育；提起，举起；饲养，种植；"]},{"id":"e02p0909","s":"Lynette","t":"Are you saying I'm a bad mother?","r":true},{"id":"e02p0910","s":"Officer","t":"Ma’am, you need to get back in your car please.","r":true},{"id":"e02p0911","s":"Lynette","t":"I have no help. My husband's always away on business.","r":true,"m":["be away on business 因公出差；因公务外出"]},{"id":"e02p0912","s":"Officer","t":"I'm gonna have to ask you to step back now.","r":true,"m":["I’m gonna have to do sth 我将不得不做某事","step back 退后"]},{"id":"e02p0913","s":"Lynette","t":"My babysitter joined the witness relocation program.","r":true,"m":["babysitter n. 临时保姆","witness relocation program 证人安置计划 witness 目击者；证人；relocation n. 重新安置；再布置；变换布置 program n. 程序；计划，规划；"]},{"id":"e02p0914","s":"Lynette","t":"I haven't slept through the night in six years and for you to stand there and judge me.","r":true,"m":["through the night 整夜地，通宵地","... and (now) for you to do sth 可用于表达目的、结果或进一步的行为等，这里可以表示'偏偏还要你来…'","judge v. 判断，认为；裁判，评判；估计 n. 法官，审判官；裁判员；鉴定人 Who am I to judge?"]},{"id":"e02p0915","s":"Officer","t":"OK. I'm not gonna give you a ticket. I'm just gonna let you off with a warning.","r":true,"m":["give you a ticket 给你开一张罚单；给你一张票 交通场景 ticket = 违章罚单","let sb off with sth 对某人从轻处罚；放过某人"]},{"id":"e02p0916","s":"Lynette","t":"I accept your apology.","r":true,"m":["apology n. 道歉"]}]},{"id":"p10","title":"Gabrielle 去 John 家里","lines":[{"id":"e02p1001","s":"John","t":"Well, this is my room. Sorry about the mess.","r":true,"m":["mess n. 肮脏，杂乱"]},{"id":"e02p1002","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Oh, don't worry about it.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1003","s":"John","t":"You just missed my mom. On Friday, she coaches my little sister's soccer team.","r":true,"m":["On Friday on + 具体某一天 Monday Tuesday Wednesday Thursday Friday Saturday Sunday","coach v. 训练，指导 n. 教练；私人教师；长途客车"]},{"id":"e02p1004","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Yes, I heard that. John, we need to talk about what happened the other day.","r":true,"m":["the other day 前几天"]},{"id":"e02p1005","s":"John","t":"Mr. Solis isn't starting to catch on, is he?","r":true,"m":["He isn't starting to catch on, is he? 他还没明白过来，是吧？","catch on 理解，领会","否定：I’m not catching on.（我没明白）","肯定：I’m starting to catch on.（我开始懂了）"]},{"id":"e02p1006","s":"Gabrielle","t":"No, he doesn't have a clue, god love him. It's just I was thinking that when you come over to garden, you might actually have to garden.","r":true,"m":["clue n. 线索，提示","He doesn't have a clue 他一无所知；他毫无头绪 I have no clue. 我一点头绪都没有","god love him 可怜他吧 / 真是拿他没办法 / 他这人啊（让人无奈又心软）","actually adv. 实际上，事实上","you might actually have to do sth 你可能实际上不得不做某事"]},{"id":"e02p1007","s":"John","t":"Great, you're breaking up with me, in my own bedroom.","r":true,"m":["break up with 分手"]},{"id":"e02p1008","s":"Gabrielle","t":"No, I'm not dumping you. Lately, you've been the only thing keeping me going. It's just we can't do it at my house anymore.","r":true,"m":["dump v. 丢弃，扔掉；乱堆，乱放；丢下，抛弃；分手，甩掉；倾销 dump sb 甩掉某人","lately adv. 近来，最近 ≈ recently"]},{"id":"e02p1009","s":"John","t":"Oh, so then, where do you want to do it?","r":true,"m":["so then 那这么说、那然后呢"]},{"id":"e02p1010","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Well, what time does your mom get back from soccer practice? You better hurry, we don't have a lot of time.","r":true,"m":["practice n. 实践，实际操作；通常的做法，惯例；练习； v. 练习，实践；美式统一用practice，英式动词用practise，名词用practice","You better hurry 口语缩写 You’d better hurry. had better + 动词原形 最好做某事","a lot of /lots of：既可接可数，也可接不可数 much + 不可数名词(much 在肯定句比较少见，大量用于否定句、疑问句) many + 可数名词复数"]}]},{"id":"p11","title":"Bree 第一次婚姻咨询","lines":[{"id":"e02p1101","s":"Bree","t":"And so there are just the four of us. My older son, Andrew, is 16, Danielle is 15 and...","r":true,"m":["older/elder son 大儿子 younger son 小儿子（little son 极少用）","older/big sister 姐姐 younger/little sister 妹妹"]},{"id":"e02p1102","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"I don't need to see pictures. Bree, you've spent most of the hour engaging in small talk.","r":true,"m":["most of the hour 这一小时里的大部分时间","engage v. 雇用，聘请；参加，从事；吸引，引起；占用 engage in 参与，从事","small talk 闲聊","engage in small talk 闲聊"]},{"id":"e02p1103","s":"Bree","t":"Oh, have I?","r":true},{"id":"e02p1104","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Yes, Rex has been very vocal about his issues. Don't you want to discuss your feelings about your marriage?","r":true,"m":["vocal adj. 直言不讳的，大声表达的；嗓音的，发声的，歌唱的","issue n. 议题，争论点；v. 发表，颁布；分发，分配","Don't you want to do sth? 你难道不想做某事吗？","discuss v. 讨论，辩论；详述，论述 discuss your feelings 谈论/探讨你的感受 talk about/express"]},{"id":"e02p1105","s":"Rex","t":"This is the thing you got to know about Bree. She doesn't like to talk about her feelings. To be honest, it's hard to know if she has any.","r":true,"m":["To be honest 老实说；说实话 actually"]},{"id":"e02p1106","s":"Rex","t":"Does she feel anger, rage, ecstasy? Who knows? She's always pleasant, and I can't tell you how annoying that is.","r":true,"m":["rage n. 盛怒，狂怒；v. 发脾气，大怒；","ecstasy n. 狂喜，陶醉","pleasant adj. 令人愉快的，和蔼可亲的","I can’t tell you how + 形容词 简直无法形容……，别提有多…… ≈ You have no idea how…","annoying adj. 令人恼火的，令人烦躁的 how annoyed I am"]},{"id":"e02p1107","s":"Rex","t":"Whatever she feels is so far below the surface, no one can see it. I feel like she's using all these domestic things..","r":true,"m":["so far below the surface 深埋在表象之下 so far 如此之深"," feel like + 从句 (that 可省略) 感觉好像……"]},{"id":"e02p1108","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Bree? Would you like to respond to what Rex just said? ","r":true},{"id":"e02p1109","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Is there some truth there? Do you use housework as a way to disengage emotionally?","r":true,"m":["Is there some truth there? 这里面有几分实情","housework n. 家务劳动，家务事 homework n.家庭作业 chores n. 家庭杂务，杂活；累活，苦差事","disengage vt. 使脱离，解开","emotionally adv. 感情上，情绪上","disengage emotionally 情感抽离、情感疏离"]},{"id":"e02p1110","s":"Bree","t":"Of course not!","r":false}]},{"id":"p12","title":"Gabrielle 意识到 John 的感情","lines":[{"id":"e02p1201","s":"John","t":"This is great. I got tons of homework tonight. It's easier to concentrate after sex.","r":true,"m":["tons of 许多;无数的;一大堆","concentrate v. 集中注意力，聚精会神；使集中，聚集；浓缩"]},{"id":"e02p1202","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I'm glad I could help. Education's very important.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1203","s":"John","t":"Oh, I got something for you. I was gonna give it to you next time I mowed your lawn, but since you're here.","r":true,"m":["since + 句子（现在时）：既然；由于 / since + 时间点：自从（完成时） / since + 句子（过去时）：自从……"]},{"id":"e02p1204","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Oh, it's a rose.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1205","s":"John","t":"It's not just any rose. Look at all the petals, there are no flaws. It's perfect. Just like you.","r":true,"m":["not just any + 单数可数名词 固定强调句型，表示“不是随便一个普通的……”，只用单数","petal n. 花瓣","flaw n. 缺点，缺陷；裂痕，瑕疵"]},{"id":"e02p1206","s":"Alice","t":"The truth hit her like a thunderbolt.","r":true,"m":["thunderbolt n. 霹雳；雷电；突发意外事件；大发雷霆  thunder n. 雷，雷声 v. 打雷 bolt n. 闪电，霹雳"]},{"id":"e02p1207","s":"John","t":"I had spent days looking for just what I wanted. Finally found it.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1208","s":"Alice","t":"For John, this was no longer a meaningless little affair. Gabrielle could now clearly see he was falling in love with her.","r":true,"m":["no longer 不再，不再是，不再存在 not … anymore","meaningless adj.无意义的；无目的的","affair n. 公共事务；私事；风流韵事；","fall in love with sb 爱上某人"]},{"id":"e02p1209","s":"Gabrielle","t":"It's just beautiful. I got to go.","r":true}]},{"id":"p13","title":"Eddie 加入 Susan 和 Mike 的晚餐","lines":[{"id":"e02p1301","s":"Susan","t":"Hey, you. What are we having?","r":true,"m":["What are we having for dinner? 晚饭我们吃什么？"]},{"id":"e02p1302","s":"Mike","t":"I talked to Julie and she suggested rib-eye steaks. She said that's your favorite.","r":true,"m":["talked to sb 和某人交谈、谈话 tell sb sth 告诉某人（某事）","rib-eye steaks 肋眼牛排 steak n.肉排，（尤指）牛排；鱼排 rib n.肋骨；排骨"]},{"id":"e02p1303","s":"Susan","t":"I love my steak.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1304","s":"Mike","t":"Eddie, Hey, I'm sorry about your house. How you holding up?","r":true,"m":["How you holding up? 你还撑得住吗 hold up 支撑，支持，举起 完整的形式应该是 \"How are you holding up?\" 这里的 \"are\" 被省略了，但在口语中，这种省略是很常见的，尤其是在非正式的场合。"]},{"id":"e02p1305","s":"Eddie","t":"All right, I guess. Oh, is somebody having a party?","r":true},{"id":"e02p1306","s":"Mike","t":"No, Susan's just throwing me one of her traditional welcome-to-the-neighborhood dinners. Only I'm cooking, and having it at my house.","r":true,"m":["throw sb a dinner 为某人举办一场晚宴；设宴招待某人; 这里的“throw”是一个俚语，意思是“举办”或“准备”，通常用于非正式的场合。","have a party/throw a party/hold a party. 举办派对","at my house：把家当作一个地点，讲活动在哪发生（吃饭、聚会、见面）in my house：强调室内，人/东西处在屋子里面。"]},{"id":"e02p1307","s":"Eddie","t":"Traditional? I didn't get one.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1308","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, it's sort of a new tradition.","r":true,"m":["sort of 有点、稍微、算得上 some sort of + 名词 = a kind of 某一种、某种"]},{"id":"e02p1309","s":"Mike","t":"It won't be anything fancy. Just a little home cooking.","r":true,"m":["fancy adj. 时髦的，奢华的；华丽的，花哨的；复杂的 v. 喜欢，想要","a little 一点儿；少量，表示肯定的意思 little 很少；几乎没有，带有否定的意味。"]},{"id":"e02p1310","s":"Eddie","t":"That sounds so good. I've been having nothing but fast food lately.","r":true,"m":["nothing but 只有；仅仅；只不过"]},{"id":"e02p1311","s":"Alice","t":"Susan suddenly had an awful feeling in the pit of her stomach. ","r":true,"m":["in the pit of her stomach 在她的胃里 pit n.坑，洼；疤痕，凹陷 v. 使竞争，使对立；这个短语通常形容一种深深的不安或恐惧感，就像在胃里有一个坑一样。"]},{"id":"e02p1312","s":"Alice","t":"As if she was watching an accident in slow motion. She knew it would happen, but was powerless to stop it.","r":true,"m":["as if 好像，仿佛。从句内容不是事实、想象出来的用虚拟语气","As if she was watching… 正式虚拟语气中应该用 were，但口语中常用 was","in slow motion 以慢动作的方式"]},{"id":"e02p1313","s":"Susan","t":"Eddie, would you like to join us for dinner?","r":true},{"id":"e02p1314","s":"Eddie","t":"Oh, that's so sweet. No, I don't want to intrude, three's a crowd.","r":true,"m":["intrude  v.闯入；打扰，侵扰；","intrude：场合介入；interrupt：打断进程、说话；disturb：扰乱安宁。","Two's company, three's a crowd. 两人作伴，三人添乱。"]},{"id":"e02p1315","s":"Mike","t":"No, it's not like that. I mean, Susan's bringing Julie.","r":true,"m":["it's not like that 不是那样的；并非如此 It doesn’t sound like that."]},{"id":"e02p1316","s":"Susan","t":"It's not like that. The more the merrier.","r":true,"m":["The more the merrier 越多越好，多多益善。通常用来表示欢迎更多的人参与某件事情 merry adj.<旧>愉快的，高兴的；<旧>令人愉快的"]},{"id":"e02p1317","s":"Eddie","t":"Well, this will be fun.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1318","s":"Mike","t":"All right, tomorrow night. We'll eat at six.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1319","s":"Eddie","t":"Great. Oh, Susan, this will make up for the dinner that you never threw me.","r":true,"m":["make up for 弥补，补偿，抵消"]},{"id":"e02p1320","s":"Mike","t":"Should I have told her we were having steak? She's not a vegetarian or something similar?","r":true,"m":["Should I have told sb sth? 我本应该告诉某人某事吗？","vegetarian n. 素食者，素食主义者；食草动物 adj. 素食的，素的","or something similar或者类似的事物；或诸如此类的东西 = or anything like that"]},{"id":"e02p1321","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, no. Eddie's definitely a carnivore.","r":true,"m":["definitely adv. 肯定地，当然；明确地，确定地","carnivore n. 食肉动物；喜欢吃肉的人，食肉动物 carnival n. 狂欢节，嘉年华会"]}]},{"id":"p14","title":"Huber 向 Lynette 收集旧衣","lines":[{"id":"e02p1401","s":"Lynette","t":"Here's what I pulled for Eddie. I should warn you that most of the clothes in there aren't that stylish.","r":true,"m":["stylish adj. 时髦的，流行的，有格调的；潇洒的"]},{"id":"e02p1402","s":"Huber","t":"Don't worry about it. Eddie's a beggar now, which means she can't be a chooser. Of course, we don't have to add salt to the wound.","r":true,"m":["beggar n. 乞丐，叫花子；","Beggars can’t be choosers. 乞丐没得挑。","add salt to the wound 在伤口上撒盐 wound n. 创伤，伤口；损害，痛苦"]},{"id":"e02p1403","s":"Lynette","t":"Listen, I was just getting dinner ready...","r":true,"m":["get ready 准备好 get sth ready 把某物准备好"]},{"id":"e02p1404","s":"Huber","t":"Say no more. I'll get out of your hair. By the way, was that you I saw getting pulled over by a policeman?","r":true,"m":["say no more 不必再说了","get out of your hair 不打扰你了，不再烦扰你，让你一个人待着。","by the way 顺便说一下","see sb getting done 看到某人被… see sb doing 看见某人正在做…","get pulled over by a policeman 被警察拦下  get pulled over通常用来描述司机被警察拦下的情况。pull over: 靠边停车"]},{"id":"e02p1405","s":"Lynette","t":"Yeah, the boys were acting up in the car, I couldn't get them to sit down.","r":true,"m":["were acting up 口语连读成 /ˈrækɪŋ ʌp/ 这种感觉","get sb to do sth 让某人做某事；使某人做某事"]},{"id":"e02p1406","s":"Huber","t":"Young boys can be so willful.","r":true,"m":["willful adj. 有意的；任性的；故意的（中性偏负面），只适合修饰人"]},{"id":"e02p1407","s":"Lynette","t":"I try everything. I scream, I threaten, I reason, I beg, nothing works.","r":true,"m":["scream v. 尖叫；高声喊，大声叫；"]},{"id":"e02p1408","s":"Lynette","t":"I don't know if it's because they're too young and they don't understand, or if they're just getting some perverse joy out of testing me.","r":true,"m":["perverse adj. 任性的，故意作对的；有悖常理的，反常的，不合人意的（强烈贬义），可以修饰人，也可以修饰感受、行为","joy n. 欢欣，高兴；使人高兴的人（或物），乐趣；成功，满足","get joy out of 固定搭配，意思是“从……中获得乐趣” get...out of... 表示从…中获得…"]},{"id":"e02p1409","s":"Huber","t":"My mother used to have the worst time with me in the car, so one time when I was acting up, she stopped and left me on the side of the road, and she drove off.","r":true,"m":["one time when...有一次当…… 的时候","on the side of the road 在路边 == by the side of the road","drive off 驾车离去"]},{"id":"e02p1410","s":"Lynette","t":"You're kidding.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1411","s":"Huber","t":"Oh, she came back immediately, but I never misbehaved in the car again. You should try that.","r":true,"m":["immediately adv. 立即，马上；紧接地，紧靠地；直接地","misbehave v. 行为不端，举止失礼；发生故障，失灵"]},{"id":"e02p1412","s":"Lynette","t":"Mrs. Huber, I could never leave my kids by the side of the road.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1413","s":"Huber","t":"When it comes to discipline, sometimes you must be creative. My mother knew that, smart lady.","r":true,"m":["discipline n/v. 纪律，风纪；惩罚；训导；训练，锻炼；科目，学科","creative adj. 创造（性）的，创作的；有创造力的，有想象力的"]},{"id":"e02p1414","s":"Huber","t":"Of course, she's in a home now, and her mind has just turned to mush.","r":true,"m":["she's in a home now, and her mind has just turned to mush. 她现在住在养老院，她的思想变得一团糟。in a home 通常表示她现在在某个住所（可能是养老院、福利院等类似的机构场所，也可能只是普通的别人家或某个居住的地方）","turn to mush 变得软糊；引申为形容人的头脑等变得混乱糊涂","mush n. 感伤的话；浓粥；软块；胆怯"]},{"id":"e02p1415","s":"Lynette","t":"Well, like I said, I should go back and get dinner ready.","r":true,"m":["like I said 就像我说的;正如我所说。书面标准：As I said"]}]},{"id":"p15","title":"Susan 看望 Paul","lines":[{"id":"e02p1501","s":"Huber","t":"Susan, have you been able to find old clothes for Eddie? She has nothing to wear.","r":true,"m":["have you been able to do sth for sb? 到目前为止，你有没有能够做到… be able to do sth for sb 能够为某人做某事"]},{"id":"e02p1502","s":"Susan","t":"I thought that was the look she was going for.","r":true,"m":["go for 追求、想要 I thought that was the look she wanted."]},{"id":"e02p1503","s":"Huber","t":"Oh, Susan, Eddie may be trash, but she is still a human being.","r":true,"m":["trash n. 垃圾，废物；","human being 人类，这里可替换为 a person，但不可以用 people，因为它指的是人们，是复数名词"]},{"id":"e02p1504","s":"Susan","t":"Zach, is your dad home? I need to talk to him. Hi, Paul, I hope I'm not interrupting.","r":true,"m":["intrude：场合介入；interrupt：打断进程、说话；disturb：扰乱安宁。"]},{"id":"e02p1505","s":"Paul","t":"Actually, I was getting ready to go somewhere.","r":true,"m":["get ready to do sth 准备好去做某事 get + adj：进入某种状态","get ready：动作，正在着手做准备的过程 be ready：状态，已经准备好了"]},{"id":"e02p1506","s":"Susan","t":"I just wanted to come by and say hello. You know, see how you guys are doing.","r":true,"m":["come by 过来拜访，顺便访问 stop by：顺路中途停下拜访","see how you guys are doing 常见的英语表达，意思是“看看你们怎么样了” How are you doing?","问人过得好不好用 how are sb doing；问事情进展用 how is sth going。"]},{"id":"e02p1507","s":"Paul","t":"We're trying to move on, it's been pretty tough.","r":true,"m":["move on 继续前进","tough adj. 坚韧的，坚固的；困难的，棘手的；艰难的，困苦的，难熬的；"]},{"id":"e02p1508","s":"Susan","t":"I can only imagine, not knowing why Mary Alice...","r":true,"m":["Not knowing 不知道, 现在分词短语作状语"]},{"id":"e02p1509","s":"Paul","t":"Why what?","r":true},{"id":"e02p1510","s":"Susan","t":"Why she did it. Oh, let me help you.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1511","s":"Paul","t":"I got it. I've got it.","r":true,"m":["I’ve got it / I got it.：两层：①我搞得定（拒绝帮忙）②我明白了"]},{"id":"e02p1512","s":"Susan","t":"I'm sorry if I upset you.","r":true,"m":["upset -> upset -> upset v. 使心烦意乱，使生气 I'm upset. It's upsetting."]},{"id":"e02p1513","s":"Paul","t":"Can I be frank?","r":true,"m":["frank adj. 坦率的，直言不讳的；明白无误的，症状明显的","Can I be frank? 我能坦率地说吗？"]},{"id":"e02p1514","s":"Susan","t":"Of course.","r":false},{"id":"e02p1515","s":"Paul","t":"I don't care what her reasons were. Maybe she was depressed, maybe she was bored, it doesn't matter.","r":true,"m":["depress v. 使抑郁，使沮丧；降低，抑制；使萧条，使不景气；按下，压下"]},{"id":"e02p1516","s":"Paul","t":"She abandoned her husband and her son, and I'll never forgive her.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1517","s":"Alice","t":"As I watched Susan, I couldn't help feeling sorry for her. She wanted so much to know why I did it, why I killed myself.","r":true,"m":["can’t/couldn’t help doing sth 情不自禁、不由得做某事","feel sorry for sb 同情某人，为某人感到难过","want so much to do sth 心里十分渴望做某事。 really want"]},{"id":"e02p1518","s":"Alice","t":"It's not enough to want the truth, you must know where to look for it. And the truth is elusive, because it knows where to hide.","r":true,"m":["look for 查找,寻找（强调寻找的过程）","elusive adj. 难以理解的，难以记住的；难以发现的，难以捕获的"]}]},{"id":"p16","title":"Huber 发现 Susan 的量杯","lines":[{"id":"e02p1601","s":"Huber","t":"Hello, Julie. I talked to your mom about donating some clothes for Eddie.","r":true,"m":["donate v. 捐赠，赠送"]},{"id":"e02p1602","s":"Julie","t":"She's at Mrs. Van De Kamp's. But I'll see if she left some stuff upstairs.","r":true,"m":["at + 人名所有格：在某某家里，省略 house。","stuff n. 东西，物品；基本特征，特质","upstairs adv. 往楼上，在楼上；脑力上，精神上"]},{"id":"e02p1603","s":"Huber","t":"Oh, Julie. I was just admiring your new measuring cup.","r":true,"m":["admire v. 钦佩，仰慕；欣赏，观赏 appreciate 多用于：感谢；鉴赏艺术、美景。"]},{"id":"e02p1604","s":"Julie","t":"Yeah, we lost ours.","r":true,"m":["ours pron.我们的，属于我们的"]},{"id":"e02p1605","s":"Huber","t":"Really?","r":false},{"id":"e02p1606","s":"Julie","t":"So I couldn't find the clothes, I'm sorry.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1607","s":"Huber","t":"That's okay.","r":false},{"id":"e02p1608","s":"Julie","t":"If you want me to keep looking?","r":true,"m":["完整陈述句：If you want me to keep looking, I can."]},{"id":"e02p1609","s":"Huber","t":"No, you've done more than enough. Truly.","r":true,"m":["more than enough 超过所需的数量或程度","you've done more than enough. 你做得已经够多了","truly adv. 真实地，如实地；真正地，完全地；真诚地；准确地；非常，很"]}]},{"id":"p17","title":"Bree 单独见 Dr. Goldfine","lines":[{"id":"e02p1701","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Bree, Rex just called. He won't be able to meet you here today, apparently, there was an emergency at the hospital.","r":true,"m":["be able to 能够、有能力做某事","emergency n. 突发事件，紧急情况；急诊病人 emerge一件事情突然冒出来、意外浮现出来 → 突发意外事件 → 紧急突发事件。"]},{"id":"e02p1702","s":"Bree","t":"Oh, Well, I wish he'd called me.","r":true,"m":["wish + had done，对过去事情的虚拟，过去没做。对将来（期盼未来）：wish + would do。 对现在正在进行：wish + were/was doing"]},{"id":"e02p1703","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"He suggested perhaps you'd like to meet with me by yourself? You've been very quiet in our joint sessions.","r":true,"m":["perhaps adv. 可能；也许 maybe","would like to 想要或希望做某事","meet sb 普通见面 vs meet with sb 有目的正式会面","by yourself 独自，自己 on your own","joint adj. 联合的，共同的，共有的；连带的","session. （某项活动的）一段时间，一场；会议，开庭；学年，上课时间；in session 会议进行中：正在进行正式会议的过程。"]},{"id":"e02p1704","s":"Bree","t":"What? No, thank you. I have some things that I need to do today.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1705","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Are you sure?","r":false},{"id":"e02p1706","s":"Bree","t":"Yeah, I'm sure.","r":false},{"id":"e02p1707","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"OK.","r":false},{"id":"e02p1708","s":"Bree","t":"Dr. Goldfine, there is something you can do for me.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1709","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"What's that?","r":false},{"id":"e02p1710","s":"Bree","t":"Take off your coat.","r":true,"m":["take off your coat 脱下你的外套 take off 脱下; 起飞; 脱离; 扣除; 模仿 coat n. 外套，大衣；","take off your clothes 脱掉你的衣服"]}]},{"id":"p18","title":"Susan 和 Gabrielle 购物聊天","lines":[{"id":"e02p1801","s":"Gabrielle","t":"So now you're taking Julie on your dinner date with Mike?","r":true,"m":["on + （活动类名词：date, trip, holiday, vacation），表示置身于这场活动当中"]},{"id":"e02p1802","s":"Susan","t":"Yeah, Well, if Eddie is gonna be there, I'm gonna need emotional support.","r":true,"m":["emotional support 情感支持 emotional adj. 情感的，情绪的。中文表达 emo"]},{"id":"e02p1803","s":"Gabrielle","t":"I can't believe she wormed her way in. How did you let her do that?","r":true,"m":["worm one's way in 像虫子一样蜿蜒前行、蠕动着进入，常引申为慢慢地、巧妙地或不择手段地渗入、钻进、混入","worm n. 蠕虫；幼虫  v. 蠕动，曲折行进"]},{"id":"e02p1804","s":"Susan","t":"I don't know, I was gonna take her out at the knees, but it all happened so fast.","r":true,"m":["take sb out at the knees 从膝盖处把她弄倒; 用来表示（通过某种手段）使某人失去能力、削弱某人的优势、击败或挫败某人"]},{"id":"e02p1805","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Well, you know what you need to do. You need to get there early, spend a little time with Mike before the little barracuda gets there.","r":true,"m":["barracuda n. 梭鱼类，是一种凶猛的食肉鱼，以其攻击性和快速游动而闻名。"]},{"id":"e02p1806","s":"Susan","t":"That's a good idea. Eddie will get there at 5:45, which means her breasts will arrive at 5:30, so I should shoot for 5:00.","r":true,"m":["breast n. 胸部，胸脯；内心 chest = 胸膛（整个胸口）","shoot for sth 以…… 为目标；力求达到；争取做到 shoot v. 开（枪），射击"]},{"id":"e02p1807","s":"Gabrielle","t":"That a girl. I'm just gonna take these upstairs.","r":true,"m":["That’s a girl. 口语省略，鼓励或赞扬女性的行为或成就。翻译为“好样的”或“这才是好女孩”","upstairs adv. 往楼上，在楼上；脑力上，精神上"]},{"id":"e02p1808","s":"Susan","t":"I'm gonna keep my one little bag and go home. That is a beautiful rose, Where did you get it?","r":true},{"id":"e02p1809","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Oh, John gave it to me.","r":true},{"id":"e02p1810","s":"Susan","t":"John? Your gardener, he gave you a rose?","r":true},{"id":"e02p1811","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Yes, I am having some new bushes planted outside, and he gave me that as a color palette.","r":true,"m":["have sth done 让 / 请别人做某事，不是自己亲手做 have sth 有某物 done 被做","palette n. 调色板；选项板；一组音调，音色"]},{"id":"e02p1812","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, OK, sure is beautiful, isn't it?","r":true,"m":["sure is beautiful 确实很美。完整的句子It sure is beautiful,省略了主语it。","sure作副词是非正式美式口语，certainly是通用副词，口语书面都可用。","It certainly is beautiful = It is certainly beautiful = Certainly it is beautiful","口语里 sure 临时充当副词（非正式），只两种常见: It sure is beautiful./ Sure, it is beautiful."]},{"id":"e02p1813","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Yes, it is.","r":false}]},{"id":"p19","title":"Bree 谈论 Freud ","lines":[{"id":"e02p1901","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"I'm sure Freud would not approve of this.","r":true,"m":["approve of 赞成、支持或认可某人或某事物 approve v. 同意，赞成；批准，通过；核准；喜欢，赞赏；approve作赞成；同意；认可讲时，是不及物动词，后面若要接宾语，需要搭配介词of，即approve of sth./sb.赞成某事 / 认可某人。","只有当approve作批准；通过讲时，才是及物动词，可以直接接宾语。The manager approved the proposal. 经理批准了这份提案。"]},{"id":"e02p1902","s":"Bree","t":"Oh, who cares what he thinks? I took psychology in college, we learned all about Freud, a miserable human being.","r":true,"m":["psychology n. 心理学；心理特点 take psychology修心理学；学习心理学","take + 学科（美口语）：大学修过这门课 = study","in college 在大学里 university 多用于学校名字，指大型综合大学","miserable adj. 痛苦的，使人难受的；糟糕的，差劲的"]},{"id":"e02p1903","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"What makes you say that?","r":true},{"id":"e02p1904","s":"Bree","t":"Well, think about it, he grew up in the late 1800s, there were no appliances back then.","r":true,"m":["grow up 长大","the late 1800s 十九世纪晚期(eighteen hundreds) ","the 1800s(1800‑1899) == the 19th century 19世纪","appliance n. 家用电器，装置 application(App)软件","back then 当时：指过去的某个时间点或时期。"]},{"id":"e02p1905","s":"Bree","t":"His mother had to do everything by hand, just backbreaking work from sunup to sundown, not to mention the countless other sacrifices she probably had to make to take care of her family.","r":true,"m":["just backbreaking work from sunup to sundown 在正式写作中可以写成 and it was just backbreaking work from sunup to sundown，逻辑更清晰, it指代前面母亲手工做所有事情这件事","backbreaking adj. 非常辛劳的；费力的","from sunup to sundown 从早到晚","countless adj. 无数的，数不尽的","sacrifice n. 牺牲，献出；献祭，供奉；祭牲"]},{"id":"e02p1906","s":"Bree","t":"And what does he do? He grows up and becomes famous, peddling a theory that the problems of most adults can be traced back to something awful their mother had done.","r":true,"m":["peddle v. 宣传，散布（思想或消息）；挨户销售，巡回销售","theory n. 学说，理论；（某一学科基于的）理论，原理；观点，见解","trace back 追溯：追寻某事物的起源或历史。回溯：回顾过去的事件或经历。","be traced back to sth 追溯到某事 / 某物","grows up and becomes 叙事性一般现在时，讲故事，把过去发生的故事改用现在时讲述，增强画面感，戏剧、小说、剧本很常见"]},{"id":"e02p1907","s":"Bree","t":"She must've felt so betrayed. He saw how hard she worked, he saw what she did for him, did he even ever think to say thank you? I doubt it.","r":true,"m":["must have done 对过去情况的肯定推测:一定做过某事；想必做过某事","betray v. 背叛，出卖；食言，辜负；违背"]},{"id":"e02p1908","s":"Bree","t":"There you go.","r":true,"m":["there you go 给你 Here you go"]},{"id":"e02p1909","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Just so you know, many of Freud's theories have been discredited.","r":true,"m":["just so you know 只是想让你知道；顺便告诉你","many Freud's theories 说法错误。名词前面有 the /my/his / Freud's 这类限定词，表示特定那一批，many 后面要加 of：many of +限定词+复数名词。没有限定词，直接：many +复数名词","discredit vt. 不信；使……丢脸 n. 怀疑；无信用；名声的败坏 credit n. 信用，信贷，赊购；赞扬，信誉，声望；v. 相信，信任"]},{"id":"e02p1910","s":"Bree","t":"Good.","r":false}]},{"id":"p20","title":"Lynette 将孩子丢在路边","lines":[{"id":"e02p2001","s":"Lynette","t":"boys, I am not gonna tell you again, sit. I mean it, I am serious. You guys are gonna be in so much trouble if you don't sit back in those seats.","r":true,"m":["I mean it 我是认真的","be in trouble 处于某种麻烦的状态中 get (into) trouble 招致、得到麻烦","sit back 坐回"]},{"id":"e02p2002","s":"Alice","t":"For the first time, Lynette could see this was not the innocent play of children, she was being challenged. So she decided it was time to get creative.","r":true,"m":["For the first time 第一次 for the last time 最后一次","innocent adj. 天真的，幼稚的；清白的，无罪的；","it was time to do sth. 是做某事的时候了","get creative 发挥创造力，尝试新的想法或方法。"]},{"id":"e02p2003","s":"Lynette","t":"Out! You can't behave? You heard me, you cannot ride. you, out, move it.","r":true,"m":["你不听话是吧？我说得很清楚，你就不能坐（这车）。ride在这里是乘坐的意思","You can’t behave? 你不能守规矩 / 你不听话？","you heard me 我说得很清楚、你听见了（强调语气）","move it 快点；赶紧；动起来。字面意思还有把它挪开/移开，但这里不是这个意思。"]},{"id":"e02p2004","s":"Children","t":"Where is she going?","r":true},{"id":"e02p2005","s":"Lynette","t":"OK, mommy is a genius, five, six, all right. Uh, mommy will be right back.","r":true,"m":["genius n. 天赋，天资；天才","right adv.此处表程度：立刻、马上，修饰后面的 back(地点副词)"]},{"id":"e02p2006","s":"Lynette","t":"Boys? If you're hiding, you've got to stop now, 'cause mommy doesn't think it's funny.","r":true,"m":["'cause（口语缩略）= because；cause 是独立单词，表示原因；导致"]},{"id":"e02p2007","s":"Lynette","t":"Oh, excuse me. I'm sorry, I'm looking for my boys, three boys with red hair, have you seen them?","r":true,"m":["with + 外貌：长着……样貌"]},{"id":"e02p2008","s":"Lady","t":"Yeah, I also saw you drive away and leave them.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2009","s":"Lynette","t":"I know，I was just trying to scare them into behaving, did you see where they went?","r":true,"m":["scare sb. into doing sth. 吓唬某人使其做某事 scare sb into behaving  吓唬某人使其守规矩"]},{"id":"e02p2010","s":"Lady","t":"Yeah, they're in my kitchen, listen, it seems to me that you have some anger management issues.","r":true,"m":["it seems to me that...看现象得到印象，在我看来……；给我的感觉好像是……","It seems that + 从句（It seems that it is true.） == It seems to be + 名词 / 形容词（It seems to be true.）","anger management 愤怒管理，情绪控制"]},{"id":"e02p2011","s":"Lynette","t":"I have four kids under the age of six, I absolutely have anger management issues.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2012","s":"Lady","t":"I think you need to talk to somebody because abandoning your children.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2013","s":"Lynette","t":"I didn't abandon them, I came back.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2014","s":"Lady","t":"I'm just saying it's not normal.","r":true,"m":["I'm just saying 我只是说一下：用于强调自己只是提供意见或建议，而不是要求别人采取行动或做出决定。"]},{"id":"e02p2015","s":"Lynette","t":"Well. my kids aren't normal, and now I don't have time for this, lady. So, boys, get out here.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2016","s":"Lady","t":"I don't think they should go anywhere until you calm down.","r":true,"m":["calm down 冷静下来"]},{"id":"e02p2017","s":"Lynette","t":"Get in the car.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2018","s":"Children","t":"She's got cookies.","r":true,"m":["She's got cookies.她有饼干have got在口语中很常用，表示拥有==have"]},{"id":"e02p2019","s":"Lynette","t":"Well, bring them, we're leaving.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2020","s":"Lady","t":"No, stay put.","r":true,"m":["stay put 不动；待在原地"]},{"id":"e02p2021","s":"Lynette","t":"Oh, I don't think so.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2022","s":"Lady","t":"Listen, lady, you and I are gonna talk.","r":false},{"id":"e02p2023","s":"Children","t":"Leave my mommy alone.","r":false,"m":["leave sb alone 不要打扰某人：不去干扰、改变或触碰某人。"]},{"id":"e02p2024","s":"Lynette","t":"Let go of me. What's the matter with you? Run, boys, run! Come on! Oh, crap.","r":true,"m":["let go of me 放开我，松手","What's the matter with you? 你怎么了？== what’s wrong (with you)?"]},{"id":"e02p2025","s":"Lynette","t":"Boys, you're gonna need to put on your...","r":false},{"id":"e02p2026","s":"Lady","t":"You get back here. Get back or I'm gonna call social services.","r":true,"m":["or 否则，要不然；或者","social services 社会服务，剧中特指（负责儿童保护的）社会福利机构"]}]},{"id":"p21","title":"Carlos 送车给 Gabrielle","lines":[{"id":"e02p2101","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Oh my god, Carlos, what have you done?","r":true},{"id":"e02p2102","s":"Carlos","t":"I saw it when I drove by dealership, I thought Gabrielle would look so beautiful in this. Cost me an arm and a leg.","r":true,"m":["drive by (sth) 开车经过…","dealership n. 特许经销商（店）（尤指汽车经销商）","Cost me an arm and a leg. 这可花了我一大笔钱。用于形容某物价格极其昂贵。"]},{"id":"e02p2103","s":"Carlos","t":"It's got GPS navigation, 200 watt stereo system, rear parking sensors.","r":true,"m":["GPS navigation gps导航","watt n. 瓦，瓦特（电功率单位）","stereo n. 立体声；立体声音响设备 stereo system 立体声音响系统","rear n. 后部，背部 adj. 后方的，背部的 v. 养育，饲养；栽种；adv. 在后面","sensor n. （探测光、热、压力等的）传感器，敏感元件，探测设备","rear parking sensors 倒车雷达或泊车辅助系统"]},{"id":"e02p2104","s":"Gabrielle","t":"God, it's beautiful.","r":false},{"id":"e02p2105","s":"Carlos","t":"So did I take your breath away?","r":true,"m":["take your breath away 形容某事或某人非常令人惊叹、震撼或感动，以至于让人无法呼吸。"]},{"id":"e02p2106","s":"Gabrielle","t":"Absolutely.","r":false},{"id":"e02p2107","s":"Carlos","t":"Is it the best gift you've ever gotten?","r":true,"m":["get-> got->got(英)/gotten(美) 但是have got表示有的意思时就用got。只有表示得到时才用gotten，但口语中还是可以用got。"]},{"id":"e02p2108","s":"Alice","t":"Gabrielle could see what this gesture had cost Carlos, so she responded the only way she knew how.","r":true,"m":["what 引导的宾语从句","gesture n. 手势，姿势；姿态，表示 V. 打手势，用动作示意","she responded the only way (that) she knew how (to respond) 省略了that的定语从句"]},{"id":"e02p2109","s":"Alice","t":"She had a feeling the truth would've been lost on her husband anyway. After all, it's the rare man who understands the value of a single perfect rose.","r":true,"m":["她当时有种感觉，就算那时候把真相告诉丈夫，他反正也理解不了。","would’ve been = would have been 对过去的虚拟，事情并未真实发生","be lost on sb 未被某人理解；对某人不起作用","rare adj.少见的，不常发生的；稀罕的 the rare man 这样少有的、不寻常的人 it's the rare man who ... 是一个强调句型, 很少有人..."]}]},{"id":"p22","title":"Susan 和 Eddie 第一回合开始","lines":[{"id":"e02p2201","s":"Susan","t":"I hope you don't mind, I thought I'd come by early and help you set up.","r":true,"m":["set up 筹备；建立，设立；安装"]},{"id":"e02p2202","s":"Eddie","t":"Hey, Susan, don't worry, Mike and I have got everything under control.","r":true,"m":["get 造成/进入某种状态 have got/gotten 现在完成时 I've got everything under control.一切尽在我掌握；我已经把局面稳住了。","under control 处于控制之下；情况正常"]},{"id":"e02p2203","s":"Mike","t":"Bongo! I don't know why he barks at you.","r":true,"m":["bark v. 大声嚷，吼叫；n. 狗叫声，吠声； bark at 对……吠叫"]},{"id":"e02p2204","s":"Eddie","t":"I wouldn't take it personally； dogs are very sensitive.","r":true,"m":["I wouldn't take it personally 你别往心里去；别把这件事当成针对你个人的。","sensitive adj. 过敏的，易受影响的；灵敏的；善解人意的，体恤的；敏感的"]},{"id":"e02p2205","s":"Eddie","t":"What's up, Bongo? You never know what freaks them out, huh?","r":true,"m":["freak n. 怪人，怪胎；怪异的事 v. <非正式>（使）吃惊，不安，恼怒 freak out 惊慌失措, 失去理智"]},{"id":"e02p2206","s":"Alice","t":"In the distance, Susan thought she heard a bell ring.","r":true,"m":["In the distance 在远处 distance n. 远处；疏远，隔阂；差距；进展；距离 v. 疏远，远离","hear->heard->heard 听到 listen 听 sound 听起来 / see 看见的结果 look 主动看的动作","bell n. 钟，铃；钟声，铃声 ring v.敲钟，按铃 hear + 物 + do：听见某物做了某个动作","她听见铃铛响了。she heard a bell/ring. 她听见了铃声"]},{"id":"e02p2207","s":"Eddie","t":"Is it a strange noise? What is it? A weird smell?","r":true,"m":["noise n. 噪音，嘈杂声；声音，响声；"]},{"id":"e02p2208","s":"Alice","t":"Round one had started.","r":true,"m":["Round one 第一轮或第一阶段"]}]},{"id":"p23","title":"Goldfine 反问 Rex","lines":[{"id":"e02p2301","s":"Rex","t":"Look, all I'm saying is that this whole it takes two to mess up a marriage theory is bull; the problems that we have are because of her.","r":true,"m":["all I'm saying is that... 我所说的全部就是……；我只是想说……","it takes two to... 表示…是双方的事；双方都有责任 it takes two to tango（一个巴掌拍不响）","mess up 弄糟；破坏；搞砸 mess n. 肮脏，杂乱 v. 弄脏，弄乱；","bull n. 公牛；废话，胡说八道；靶心","because of 介词短语+名词/代词 because 连词+句子"]},{"id":"e02p2302","s":"Bree","t":"That is not true, Rex.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2303","s":"Rex","t":"All right, fine. What I have been doing for the past 20 years has been so awful?","r":true,"m":["What was so awful? 当时）究竟什么事那么糟糕？What has been so awful? （一直到现在）究竟是什么一直这么糟糕？","过去时：强调的是过去的那个时间；现在完成时：强调过去到现在的持续，或者对现在的影响，无需管是否完成","What I have been doing ... 是what引导的主语从句","have been doing 现在完成进行时 What have you been doing these days? 你这些天一直在做什么？I’ve been working.","现在完成时强调的是结果，现在完成进行时强调的则是过程","for the past 20 years 在过去的 20 年里"]},{"id":"e02p2304","s":"Rex","t":"You're not saying anything because I've been a great husband, and it kills you to admit that.","r":true,"m":["It kills sb to admit sth 让某人承认某事真的很难受（或很痛苦、很煎熬）"]},{"id":"e02p2305","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Rex, I'm curious, do you ever acknowledge the benefits of living with Bree?","r":true,"m":["curious adj. 好奇的，求知欲强的；稀奇的，不寻常的；爱挑剔的","acknowledge v. 承认；正视、认可 admit 承认（过错）knowledge n. 知识，学问；知道，了解","the benefits of sth 某事 / 某物的益处、好处"]},{"id":"e02p2306","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"By your own admission, your home's always clean; your clothes are always freshly pressed; she sounds like a wonderful cook.","r":true,"m":["By your own admission 据你自己所说 admission n. 承认，供认","freshly adv. 新近；精神饱满地 pressed adj. （时间、资金等）紧缺的；压平的，压扁的 freshly pressed  刚压榨的；刚熨烫的","sound like + n.：听起来像…；听起来仿佛是… sound + adj：听起来… Her cooking sounds wonderful."]},{"id":"e02p2307","s":"Dr. Goldfine","t":"Despite her flaws, do you ever remember to say thank you?","r":true,"m":["despite prep. 尽管，即使；不由自主地，忍不住地 Although she has flaws","flaw n. 缺点，缺陷；裂痕，瑕疵 v. 削弱，使失效"]}]},{"id":"p24","title":"Susan 和 Eddie 第二回合","lines":[{"id":"e02p2401","s":"Mike","t":"Bongo! Get down! Down! I'm sorry. So who's the guy that lives across from Mrs. Huber again?","r":true,"m":["live across from 地点 住在...的对面 live across the street 住在街对面","that lives / who lives 尽量不重复用who / living"]},{"id":"e02p2402","s":"Susan","t":"That's Mr. Mullen. And just so you know, if he invites you in, you have to meet all of his pets.","r":true,"m":["just so you know 固定口语句式：跟你说一声、顺便告诉你，用于引出提醒、忠告。","invite sb in 邀请某人进来 in是副词表示进屋 invite sb to + 地点 = If he invites you to his house"]},{"id":"e02p2403","s":"Mike","t":"That's OK, I love animals.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2404","s":"Susan","t":"He is a taxidermist.","r":true,"m":["taxidermist n. 动物标本剥制者 taxi 出租车","stuffed animals 动物标本，填充动物标本"]},{"id":"e02p2405","s":"Mike","t":"Oh, OK, thanks for the warning.","r":true,"m":["thanks(thank you) for the warning. 谢谢你的提醒。","thank you 动词 thanks 名词复数，代表多份感激、许许多多的谢意"]},{"id":"e02p2406","s":"Eddie","t":"Isn't Mr. Mullen's brother your divorce attorney?","r":true,"m":["attorney n. 律师；代理人 = lawyer divorce attorney 离婚律师，更地道","口语习惯用现在时 Isn’t … 提起过去的旧事，不需要严格时态对齐。"]},{"id":"e02p2407","s":"Susan","t":"Yes, he was.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2408","s":"Eddie","t":"Can I say something? In my heart, I still believe that you and Carl are gonna get back together.","r":true,"m":["get back together 复合"]},{"id":"e02p2409","s":"Mike","t":"Really?","r":false},{"id":"e02p2410","s":"Eddie","t":"Oh, yeah. I've never seen two people more in love. I mean, she's never gonna find that kind of chemistry with another man, never.","r":true,"m":["I've never seen two people more in love 我从未见过比他们更相爱的两个人。in love 相爱、处于恋爱中 more in love 爱得更深、更加恩爱","never 频率副词，大都放在be动词/助动词/情态动词后；实义动词前","chemistry n. 化学；化学成分，化学反应"]},{"id":"e02p2411","s":"Alice","t":"It was everything Susan could do to keep a smile on her face, round two was under way, and she was already taking a beating.","r":true,"m":["It was everything sb could do to do sth 这个句型强调某人做某事极为艰难，需要使出浑身解数才能做到","under way 进行中；已开始并进行着 = underway=going on","take a beating 遭受重创; 遭受挫折或损失"]},{"id":"e02p2412","s":"Alice","t":"What Eddie hadn’t counted on was that Susan had someone else in her corner.","r":true,"m":["count on sth/sb 料想到；指望；依靠；依赖（某事物）","in sb's corner 支持某人；站在某人一边"]},{"id":"e02p2413","s":"Julie","t":"You know what, Mrs. Britt? Do you know who I always liked? Mr. Rothwell, your fourth husband.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2414","s":"Eddie","t":"He was my second husband, I've only been married twice.","r":true,"m":["be married to sb 与某人存在婚姻关系，强调的是一种婚姻状态, be married 是一个表示婚姻状态的短语","marry sb 与某人结婚，强调的是结婚这个动作,不能用 marry to sb 来表达"]},{"id":"e02p2415","s":"Julie","t":"Twice? You weren't married to the guy with all the tattoos that they took away in handcuffs?","r":true,"m":["发音：weren't：əː → 饿 、won't：oʊ → 欧 、want：ɑː → 啊","tattoo n. 刺青，纹身 with all the tattoos/red hair 外貌特征；all the 强调：纹身遍布全身","they took away in handcuffs \"they\" 是一个泛指，用来指代那些负责执法和维护治安的人。 take away 带走","handcuff n. 手铐 in handcuffs 戴着手铐"]},{"id":"e02p2416","s":"Susan","t":"No, Julie, she wasn't married to Javier; that was just one of her special friends.","r":true,"m":["that 这里指Javier，可以用 he 来代替"]},{"id":"e02p2417","s":"Susan","t":"I think we should change the subject. You know, unless you want to keep talking about it.","r":true,"m":["change the subject 转换话题"]}]},{"id":"p25","title":"Bongo 误食耳环","lines":[{"id":"e02p2501","s":"Mike","t":"Bongo, get down.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2502","s":"Eddie","t":"Wait, let me show you something.","r":true,"m":["let me show you something 让我给你看些东西"]},{"id":"e02p2503","s":"Mike","t":"He loves that gravy.","r":true,"m":["gravy n. 肉汁；不法利润；轻易得来的钱； 作为肉汁肉卤时是不可数名词"]},{"id":"e02p2504","s":"Eddie","t":"Come, while you were in there tossing a salad, I taught him something.","r":true,"m":["toss v. 扔，抛，掷；（使）摇摆，挥动，颠簸；搅拌（食物），拌匀","toss a salad 拌一份沙拉 salad 是可数名词","teach sb sth 教某人某事 -> taught -> taught"]},{"id":"e02p2505","s":"Alice","t":"Susan was furious with Eddie for using a dog to ingratiate herself with its owner.","r":true,"m":["furious adj. 狂怒的，暴怒的 be furious with sb for doing sth 因某人做了某事而对其大发雷霆","anger和angry 普通生气。rage和enraged≈furious 暴怒，情绪失控。wrath很少用，多指有权者、神明的怒火。/ curious","ingratiate vt. 使迎合；使讨好 use sth to ingratiate oneself with sb 利用某物来讨好某人"]},{"id":"e02p2506","s":"Alice","t":"She was also furious with Mike for not seeing through this blatant maneuver.","r":true,"m":["see through 指能够透过看到背后的事物。","blatant adj. 喧嚣的；公然的；炫耀的；俗丽的","maneuver(美式) = manoeuvre(英式) n. 细致巧妙的移动，机动动作；策略，手段；军事演习","blatant maneuver 用于描述那些不道德、不正当且毫不掩饰的手段"]},{"id":"e02p2507","s":"Alice","t":"But mostly she was furious with herself for not having thought of it first.","r":true,"m":["not having thought of 当初本该先想到，却之前没有想到"]},{"id":"e02p2508","s":"Susan","t":"so, you know what? I'm gonna go get the desserts.","r":true,"m":["so, you know what? 你知道吗：用于引起某人的注意，然后宣布某事。","go get sth 去拿某物，去取某物；go + 动词原形 是美语高频口语结构，表去做某事","dessert n.甜点 desert 沙漠"]},{"id":"e02p2509","s":"Eddie","t":"You are such a smart boy!","r":true,"m":["such a/an + adj + 单数名词， such修饰名词","You are so smart (a boy)! so + adj (+ a/an + 单数名词) so修饰形容词"]},{"id":"e02p2510","s":"Mike","t":"I can barely get him to sit. I've never seen him walk on two legs.","r":true,"m":["barely adv. 勉强才能；几乎不，几乎没有；刚刚；仅仅，只有；= hardly 几乎不，侧重难度","rarely adv. 罕有，很少；异乎寻常地，极度 = seldom 很少，侧重频率","I can barely get him to sit 我几乎没办法让他坐下。get sb. to do sth 强调通过某种努力、办法或手段去促使某人做某事","I can barely let him sit 我几乎不太愿意让他坐下。let sb. do sth. 更侧重于表达一种许可、准许的态度","see sb do sth 看见某人做某事"]},{"id":"e02p2511","s":"Eddie","t":"He knows who to come to, doesn’t he?","r":true,"m":["come to sb 向某人求助；去找某人"]},{"id":"e02p2512","s":"Susan","t":"Here's your dessert.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2513","s":"Eddie","t":"Thank you, Mike, this looks yummy.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2514","s":"Mike","t":"Oh, look at that, it’s like Bongo's finally warming up to Susan.","r":true,"m":["it’s like (that)… 口语用法，好像、看样子、仿佛。","warm up to 慢慢对某人产生好感、变得亲近，放下戒备"]},{"id":"e02p2515","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, we just got off on the wrong foot; we're best buddies now. Oh, what a good boy! Bongo, are you OK?","r":true,"m":["get off on the wrong foot 一开始就做错；一开始就不顺利；出师不利","buddy n. 伙伴，好朋友","what a good boy (he is)! what引导的感叹句","how引导的感叹句: how good the boy is."]},{"id":"e02p2516","s":"Eddie","t":"What's wrong with him?","r":true},{"id":"e02p2517","s":"Mike","t":"I don't know, I never heard him make that sound. Are you OK, fella?","r":true,"m":["fella n. 伙伴，伙计；小伙子"]},{"id":"e02p2518","s":"Julie","t":"Mom? Where is your earring?","r":false,"m":["necklace项链 earring耳环 watch手表 ring戒指"]},{"id":"e02p2519","s":"Mike","t":"Call the vet, the number's on the fridge, tell him I'll be right there.","r":true,"m":["vet n. 兽医","fridge n. 冰箱","I'll be right there. 我马上就到那儿 I'll be right over. 我马上就过来。"]},{"id":"e02p2520","s":"Eddie","t":"OK, don't worry about a thing. I'll stay here and get everything cleaned up.","r":true,"m":["Don't worry about a thing 别担心任何事，什么都不用担心。== Don't worry about anything","clean up 收拾、清理残局"]},{"id":"e02p2521","s":"Mike","t":"Thanks, Eddie.","r":false},{"id":"e02p2522","s":"Susan","t":"Is there anything I can do?","r":true},{"id":"e02p2523","s":"Mike","t":"No.","r":false}]},{"id":"p26","title":"Bongo平安","lines":[{"id":"e02p2601","s":"Susan","t":"How's Bongo doing?","r":true,"m":["问人过得好不好用 how are/is sb doing；问事情进展用 how is sth going。"]},{"id":"e02p2602","s":"Mike","t":"I'm waiting to see if they'll have to operate.","r":true,"m":["operate v. 操纵，操作；开刀，动手术；"]},{"id":"e02p2603","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, god. I stopped and I got this for... I'm just so sorry for this.","r":true,"m":["stop：行进途中特意停下。"]},{"id":"e02p2604","s":"Mike","t":"I'm really sorry I snapped at you. I just...","r":true,"m":["snap at sb 对人厉声说 snap v. 厉声说,怒气冲冲地说；断裂,绷断；突然失控 yell at 大多带着愤怒情绪吼叫"]},{"id":"e02p2605","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, no, it's OK.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2606","s":"Vet","t":"Good news, we won't have to do surgery.","r":true,"m":["surgery n. 外科手术；do surgery ≈ operate"]},{"id":"e02p2607","s":"Susan","t":"Oh, that's great.","r":true},{"id":"e02p2608","s":"Vet","t":"We've given Bongo something to help pass the earring. When he does, would you like us to retrieve it for you?","r":true,"m":["help do sth 帮助做某事 == help to do sth","pass v. 排泄；经过，穿过；传递","When he does = When he passes the earring 可用 do/does/did 替代前文重复的动词"]},{"id":"e02p2609","s":"Susan","t":"I'm gonna say no.","r":true,"m":["I'm gonna say no. 那我还是算了吧，我这边就不用了"]},{"id":"e02p2610","s":"Vet","t":"OK, you should be able to take him home in about an hour.","r":true,"m":["take sb home 带某人回家","in about an hour 大约一小时后"]},{"id":"e02p2611","s":"Susan","t":"Wow, You must be so relieved.","r":true,"m":["relieved adj. 放心的，宽慰的 relieve v. 缓解；减轻"]},{"id":"e02p2612","s":"Mike","t":"I'm sorry, I was just really worried.","r":true,"m":["be worried (about sb) 表示担忧的状态"]},{"id":"e02p2613","s":"Susan","t":"It was your dog, I get it.","r":true,"m":["狗现在依旧属于对方，was 只是回溯刚刚那个场景。"]},{"id":"e02p2614","s":"Mike","t":"Actually, he was my wife's dog, and one of the last things she said to me in the hospital before she died was to be sure I looked after him, and I promised her I would.","r":true,"m":["One of the last things … was to do …某人临终 / 临走交代的几件事之一就是去做…","be sure that... 确保……；务必……","look after sb 照顾、照料某人/动物/植物 = take care of sb","take care of 还有处理活儿、解决麻烦、办妥事情的意思，此时不能替换为look after"]},{"id":"e02p2615","s":"Alice","t":"And just like that, Susan could suddenly see something she'd never seen before. Mike Delfino was still in love with his late wife.","r":true,"m":["be in love with sb 爱上某人；与某人相爱","late adj.已故的；晚期的，末期的；晚的，迟的。委婉提及已经去世的家人 → late + 亲属名词"]},{"id":"e02p2616","s":"Mike","t":"He meant so much to her. And if something had happened, I would've felt like I'd failed her. I know that sounds stupid, but...","r":true,"m":["mean so much to sb 对某人来说意义重大；对某人非常重要","If something had happened, I would've felt like I had failed her. 要是当时发生了什么事情的话，我就会觉得我已经辜负了她。对过去的虚拟","fail sb 让某人失望；有负于某人"]},{"id":"e02p2617","s":"Alice","t":"And she knew right then neither she nor Eddie would be laying claim to his heart anytime soon.","r":true,"m":["right then 就在那时；当时","neither A nor B：A 和 B 两者都不,谓语就近原则 both A and B：A 和 B 两者都,谓语用复数","would be doing 过去将来进行时，在过去的时间点看将来正在进行的动作","claim n/v. 声称，断言；索要，索赔","lay claim to sth 宣称对某物拥有所有权 lay claim to his heart 宣称赢得他的芳心；声称占据他的感情","anytime soon 很快的任何时候；近期内：表示事情不会很快改善或发生。"]},{"id":"e02p2618","s":"Alice","t":"So she decided, for now, she could settle for just being his friend.","r":true,"m":["for now 目前；暂时","settle for sth 将就，勉强接受，妥协接受某事物 settle v. 解决，结束；确定，决定；定居"]},{"id":"e02p2619","s":"Susan","t":"No, it doesn't, not at all. This is for you, well, for Bongo, you give it to him.","r":false},{"id":"e02p2620","s":"Alice","t":"Yes, as I look back at the world I left behind, it's all so clear to me, the beauty that waits to be unveiled, the mysteries that long to be uncovered.","r":true,"m":["look back at/on sth 回顾，回忆（某事）；回头看，再看（某物） look back at the world 回望这个世界；回首看世界","unveil v. （首次）公开，揭示；为…揭幕，揭去…上的覆盖物；除去面纱，显露","mystery n. 难以理解的事物，奥秘；神秘的人","uncover v. 揭露，发现；揭开盖子，移开覆盖物；发掘，挖出"]},{"id":"e02p2621","s":"Alice","t":"But people so rarely stop to take a look, they just keep moving. It's a shame, really, there's so much to see.","r":true,"m":["rarely adv. 罕有，很少；异乎寻常地，极度","stop to take a look 停下来看一眼","It's a shame 这是一件憾事 shame n. 令人惋惜的事；羞耻，羞愧；What a shame."]}]}]};
